  "name_ar": "دليل حسابات للمملكة العربية السعودية",
  "name_en": "Saudi Arabia chart of accounts",
  "countries": [
    "SA"
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "IFRS as endorsed by SOCPA, with the statutory accounts a Saudi entity needs for ZATCA VAT, Zakat, income tax, withholding tax and GOSI",
    "url": "https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Taxes/Pages/VATLaw.aspx",
    "note": "There is no national chart of accounts mandated for commercial companies in Saudi Arabia. The unified chart that does exist is for government entities and does not apply here, and this template does not pretend otherwise: its structure is the generic IFRS one, which is what SOCPA endorsed for financial reporting, and what it adds is the set of accounts a Saudi entity cannot operate without. Those are the ones driven by obligations rather than by presentation: VAT under the VAT Law and its Implementing Regulations administered by ZATCA, Zakat on the zakat base, income tax on the non-Saudi ownership share with mixed companies apportioning between the two, withholding tax on payments to non-residents, and social insurance contributions to GOSI. End-of-service benefits are an employee benefit obligation under IAS 19, required by the Labor Law. No RATE appears in this file, deliberately - rates change by regulation and belong to the tax engine, where a change is dated and a historical return still recomputes. A tenant is free to choose the generic template instead; a Saudi subsidiary keeping its books on a group chart is an ordinary arrangement."
  },
