      "type": "liability",
      "name_ar": "بضاعة مستلمة غير مفوترة",
      "name_en": "Goods received not invoiced",
      "postable": true,
      "role": "goods_received_not_invoiced",
      "monetary": true,
      "note": "PF-132: a liability for things that have arrived and whose bill has not. What makes a period-end cutoff honest, and a balance that does not clear is a receipt nobody was ever billed for."
    },
    {
      "code": "2.1.11",
      "parent": "2.1",
      "type": "liability",
      "name_ar": "مستحقات للعاملين",
      "name_en": "Employee payables",
      "postable": true,
      "role": "employee_payable",
      "monetary": true,
      "note": "PF-143: what the business owes its own people. An employee is not a supplier - the balance is reported differently, it is frequently settled through payroll, and an aging report that mixed the two would show a colleague's taxi fare beside a supplier on thirty-day terms."
    },
    {
      "code": "2.1.12",
      "parent": "2.1",
      "type": "liability",
      "name_ar": "مقبوضات غير مخصّصة",
      "name_en": "Unapplied cash",
      "postable": true,
      "role": "unapplied_cash",
      "monetary": false,
      "note": "NOT monetary. Deferred revenue is settled by delivering goods and services, not by paying money, so restating it at the closing rate puts an exchange difference through profit or loss for an obligation that is not denominated in currency. It is the account most often wrongly marked monetary."
    },
    {
      "code": "2.2",
      "parent": "2",
      "type": "liability",
